    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG is delighted to present 20 Sandymount Road, Sandymount, Dublin 4 to the market. A distinguished and exceptionally well-maintained period residence, No. 20 enjoys a prime coastal location and offers an exceptional degree of versatility. Set along the highly sought-after Sandymount Road, this elegant mid-terrace home has been carefully maintained, modernised and upgraded to an excellent standard, while retaining a wealth of original period features and character.\n\nThe location is equally impressive, with Sandymount Village, Sandymount Strand and Dublin city centre all within easy reach. The area is renowned for its village atmosphere, strong sense of community and excellent selection of amenities, while the nearby coastline provides a wonderful setting for walking and recreation.\n\nSet back from the road and approached through a pedestrian gate, the property is accessed via attractive granite steps leading to the front door. The welcoming entrance hallway immediately reveals the character and charm of the house, with a number of fine original period details retained throughout.\n\nAt hall-floor level, two elegant interconnecting reception rooms enjoy dual aspects to both the front and rear. Currently arranged as a living room and kitchen/dining room, these versatile spaces are bright and inviting, providing an ideal environment for both everyday family life and entertaining. A guest w.c. with laundry facilities completes this level, while steps with a handrail lead directly to the private rear garden.\n\nUpstairs, the first-floor return is flooded with natural light and features a magnificent window overlooking the rear garden. The main first floor comprises three generously proportioned double bedrooms, including an impressive principal bedroom with en-suite facilities, together with a well-appointed family bathroom.\n\nThe garden level provides a valuable additional dimension to the property. Also accessed independently beneath the front steps, this level features a generous entrance hall leading to a spacious bedroom. A further inner hallway provides access to the open-plan living room and kitchen, together with a newly refurbished bathroom. This level also benefits from direct access to the rear garden, making it particularly suitable for independent living, accommodating extended family or guests, or providing a quiet and ideal working from home space.\n\nThe impressive rear garden extends to a generous length and provides a private and peaceful outdoor retreat. Beautifully maintained, it is predominantly laid in lawn and incorporates a paved limestone patio, with a further granite-paved patio area towards the rear.\n\nHigh stone walls and timber fencing provide excellent privacy, while a detached garage at the end of the garden is accessed via Beach Avenue off Beach Road. The garage comfortably accommodates two vehicles and is fitted with an electric roller shutter for convenient access.\n\nSituated in the heart of Sandymount, one of Dublin's most sought-after residential locations, No. 20 enjoys an enviable combination of coastal charm and excellent urban convenience. Sandymount Village is within a short stroll and offers an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, shops and everyday amenities, while Sandymount Strand provides beautiful coastal walks and open space.\n\nTransport links are excellent, with regular bus services operating directly outside the property and providing convenient access to Dublin city centre. The DART station at Lansdowne Road is also within walking distance, offering further connectivity throughout Dublin and beyond. Families are exceptionally well catered for, with a selection of highly regarded schools in the surrounding area, including Star of the Sea National School, Shellybanks Educate Together National School, Sandymount Park Educate Together Secondary School, Lakelands Girls National School, St Matthew's National School and Marian College, among others.\n\nCombining elegant period architecture, modern upgrades, exceptionally versatile accommodation, a substantial private rear garden and a generous, detached garage, 20 Sandymount Road represents a rare opportunity to acquire a truly special home in one of Dublin's most desirable coastal neighbourhoods. With its exceptional flexibility and outstanding location, this impressive property is ideally suited to those seeking a long-term family home, an intergenerational residence with significant appeal.\n\nEarly viewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Level - \n\n\nEntrance Hall - \nwelcoming hallway with fitted carpet, fan light over door, ceiling coving and rose, hallway arch, doors leading to reception rooms. Stairs to first floor\n\nLiving Room - \ngenerous reception room, large window to front, window shutters, ceiling coving and rose, original fireplace surround with open fire, picture rail, interconnecting doors to kitchen / dining room\n\nKitchen Dining Room - \nbright reception with fitted carpet and tiled kitchen area, large window overlooking rear garden, window shutters, ceiling coving and rose, picture rail, original fireplace surround with open fire. Fitted kitchen units, tiled splashback, integrated dishwasher, electric oven, hob and extractor fan\n\nGuest w.c. - \ntiled floor, w.c. and w.h.b. with tiled splashback and mirror. Extractor fan. Plumbed for washing machine.\n\nHall Floor Return - \nlarge window overlooking rear garden\n\nFirst Floor Landing - \nspacious landing with built in storage, fitted carpet, access to attic, large Velux window, pitcure rail\n\nBedroom 1 - \ngenerous master bedroom with fitted carpet, large window to front, window shutters, picture rail, fireplace surround, built in wardrobes. Door to en-suite\n\nEn-suite - \ntiled floor and part tiled walls, shower unit, w.c., w.h.b. heated towel rail, extractor fan, recessed lights\n\nBedroom 2 - \nspacious double bedroom with fitted carpet, window to front, window shutters, built in wardrobe, picture rail, access to attic, fireplace surround\n\nBedroom 3 - \nbright double bedroom with fitted carpet, large window overlooking rear garden, window shutters, built in wardrobes, picture rail\n\nBathroom - \nTiled floor, part tiled walls, shower over bath, shower screen, w.c., w.h.b. set in cabinet, heated towel rail, recessed lights, window to rear\n\nGarden Level - \n\n\nEntrance Hall - \ngenerous hallway with newly fitted carpet, door to understep storage. Door to inner hall\n\nBedroom - \nlarge bedroom with fitted carpet, built in wardrobes, fireplace surround with tiled inset, window to front, window shutters\n\nInner Hall - \nnewly fitted carpet, doors leading to open living room / kitchen, bathroom. Fitted units with countertop and shelving, plumbed for washing machine.\n\nLiving Room / Kitchen - \nspacious reception room with fitted carpet and tiled area in kitchen, fitted kitchen units, tiled splashback, integrated dishwasher, electric oven, hob and extractor, window to rear garden, double patio doors to rear garden\n\nBathroom - \nNewly fitted bathroom, tiled floor and walls, bath, separate shower unit, window to rear, recessed lights, w.c., wh.b. heated towel rail, mirrored bathroom cabinet\n\nOutside - \n\n\nFront - \nfully railed front garden with pedestrian gate, granite path and steps to the property. Laid lawn with planted borders. On street resident parking\n\nRear Garden - \ngenerous rear garden provides a private and peaceful outdoor retreat. fully enclosed by stone wall and high fence. Beautifully maintained, it is predominantly laid in lawn and incorporates a paved limestone patio and path, with a further granite-paved patio area towards the rear.\n\nGarage - \ngenerous detached concrete block garage with three doors leading in from rear garden, power points, lighting, mains water supply and drainage. Electric roller shutter. Access from Beach Avenue off Beach Road\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Highly desirable Dublin 4 location</li><li> An exceptionally well-maintained period property in walk-in condition</li><li> Recently replaced roof, central heating system, rewired, Tuck brick pointing and windows throughout,</li><li> Spacious accommodation of 210 sq. m (2,260 sq. ft)</li><li> Elegant mid-terrace period residence in a quiet, sought-after setting</li><li> Suitable for family living, intergenerational use, or investment</li><li> Detached garage to rear with space for two cars. Accessed by Beach Avenue off Beach Road</li><li> Short walk to Sandymount Village, Sandymount Strand, and city centre</li><li> Excellent transport links and local amenities nearby</li><li> GFCH</li><li> Alarmed</ul>"
